        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1050">

                <pb facs="0211" n="1913" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p2/pg1913"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">774.5/12–1652: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1050<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary
                            of State to the Embassy in
                        Egypt</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d1050-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-12-16T18:43:00-05:00">December 16, 1952—6:43
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1227. Re Deptel 1171 to Cairo Dec 5 concerning
                    proposed Anglo-Amer talks on Egypt Rep Brit Emb Dec 15 informed along fol lines:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“FonOff wld like start these talks as
                            soon as possible after Christmas. Scope of talks (as Dept has suggested)
                            wld be: <quote rend="blockquote">
                                <p>“1. Terms upon which Her Majesty’s govt cld agree to withdraw
                                    from CZ, 2. collaboration of Arab states with MEDO, 3. mil aid to Egypt as part
                                    of gen settlement, 4. econ aid to Egypt.</p>
                            </quote></p>
                        <p>“Mr. Eden wld greatly prefer them
                            to take place in London, since the relevant info is all readily avail
                            there and since it is after all the Brit who will be putting forward
                            their ideas on the mil side at any rate.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"><hi
                                    rendition="#small-caps"
                    >Bruce</hi></hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1050-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1050-f1-content">
                <p>Also sent to London as telegram 4050 and to Khartoum as telegram 16.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
